estion/worked-solution "Using the distributive law, we multiply each term inside the parentheses by the number $(-6):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6(7x-2y) & = \\\\ (-6)\\cdot 7x+(-6)\\cdot (-2y) & = \\\\ (-42x)+(12y) & = \\\\ -42x+12y & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4415fb7e-0c64-568e-8b39-038589dcda18" "answer-field-4645ab3d-e5f1-5b30-afb6-d33ed6af0e74"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4415fb7e-0c64-568e-8b39-038589dcda18" :answer-field/id #uuid "4415fb7e-0c64-568e-8b39-038589dcda18" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d235ff94-e2a3-51a0-b6bc-81a043590012" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d235ff94-e2a3-51a0-b6bc-81a043590012"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d235ff94-e2a3-51a0-b6bc-81a043590012" :answer/id #uuid "d235ff94-e2a3-51a0-b6bc-81a043590012" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4645ab3d-e5f1-5b30-afb6-d33ed6af0e74" :answer-field/id #uuid "4645ab3d-e5f1-5b30-afb6-d33ed6af0e74" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-9320fcd8-c1a5-5442-975f-33812558c83f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9320fcd8-c1a5-5442-975f-33812558c83f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9320fcd8-c1a5-5442-975f-33812558c83f" :answer/id #uuid "9320fcd8-c1a5-5442-975f-33812558c83f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-350766c2-00ec-55fc-8f6d-53d2e27047a9" :question/id #uuid "350766c2-00ec-55fc-8f6d-53d2e27047a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-180938" :question/problem "$(8u-3v)\\cdot (-6)=${{field-1}}\n$u\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$v$" :question/worked-solution "Using the distributive law, we multiply each term inside the parentheses by the number $(-6):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(8u-3v)\\cdot (-6) & = \\\\ 8u\\cdot (-6)+(-3v)\\cdot (-6) & = \\\\ (-48u)+(18v) & = \\\\ -48u+18v & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c96f3ee8-4f07-59bc-b6be-0e3ccecf54c6" "answer-field-178cb863-e58b-53bc-988f-2a316aa3e692"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c96f3ee8-4f07-59bc-b6be-0e3ccecf54c6" :answer-field/id #uuid "c96f3ee8-4f07-59bc-b6be-0e3ccecf54c6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-68afdf8b-8873-5260-95f1-9d9dd1ddf83d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-68afdf8b-8873-5260-95f1-9d9dd1ddf83d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-68afdf8b-8873-5260-95f1-9d9dd1ddf83d" :answer/id #uuid "68afdf8b-8873-5260-95f1-9d9dd1ddf83d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-178cb863-e58b-53bc-988f-2a316aa3e692" :answer-field/id #uuid "178cb863-e58b-53bc-988f-2a316aa3e692" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-46c556cb-ebd0-5aa3-8399-2749def5dd66" :answer-field/choices ["answer-46c556cb-ebd0-5aa3-8399-2749def5dd66"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46c556cb-ebd0-5aa3-8399-2749def5dd66" :answer/id #uuid "46c556cb-ebd0-5aa3-8399-2749def5dd66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186056023 :tutorial/content "The **distributive law** states that multiplying a group of terms by a number is the same as multiplying each term separately by that same number and adding the products.\n\nFor example, let's take a look at the following expression: \n\n$$\n2(3+4).\n$$\n\n \n\nWe can evaluate this expression using the distributive law:\n\n![](images/4c/4ca32844e45f756ce88e4d8e6d73e8b69099d2c517157b51fed9bb1f02a699ea.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(3+4) & = \\\\ 2\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 4 & = \\\\ 6+8 & = \\\\ 14 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe distributive law also applies when the multiplication occurs on the right of the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3+4)\\cdot 2 & = \\\\ 3\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 2 & = \\\\ 6+8 & = \\\\ 14 & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186056024 :tutorial/content "The distributive law also works when there is subtraction inside the parentheses. \n\nFor example, we can expand the expression $2(3-4)$ as follows:\n\n![](images/05/05ba4424f566b35af2a279b994c3a8f13564560deaa60f1c7c4616f52d2fb8d6.png)\n\nNotice that we keep a plus ($+$) sign between the two terms. This helps us to avoid mistakes when multiplying with negative numbers.\n\nNow, evaluating our expression, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(3-4) & = \\\\ 2\\cdot 3+2\\cdot (-4) & = \\\\ (6)+(-8) & = \\\\ 6-8 & = \\\\ -2 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distributive law also applies when the multiplication occurs on the right of the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3-4)\\cdot 2 & = \\\\ 3\\cdot 2+(-4)\\cdot 2 & = \\\\ (6)+(-8) & = \\\\ 6-8 & = \\\\ -2 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054885 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
